---
description: Run only the Console UITests that cover the change; never the full suite
alwaysApply: true
---

# Targeted UITests only

`ConsoleUITests` launches the real app for every case. The full suite is slow and is not a default check. Run the smallest UI coverage that can fail for this change.

Prefer `ConsoleTests` (unit) when it can prove the change. Use UITests only for UI, launch, or accessibility behavior that unit tests cannot see.

## How to run

From `Console/` (the directory that contains `Console.xcodeproj`):

```bash
# One class
xcodebuild test -project Console.xcodeproj -scheme ConsoleUITests \
  -destination 'platform=macOS' \
  -only-testing:ConsoleUITests/NavigationUITests

# One method (preferred when you know it)
xcodebuild test -project Console.xcodeproj -scheme ConsoleUITests \
  -destination 'platform=macOS' \
  -only-testing:ConsoleUITests/NavigationUITests/testLaunchStartsOnHome
```

Repeat `-only-testing:` for each extra class or method. Pick classes that match the surface you changed (sidebar → `NavigationUITests`, settings → `SettingsUITests`, and so on).

## Do not

```bash
# ❌ Full UITest target
xcodebuild test -project Console.xcodeproj -scheme ConsoleUITests -destination 'platform=macOS'

# ❌ Console scheme also runs ConsoleUITests unless filtered
xcodebuild test -project Console.xcodeproj -scheme Console -destination 'platform=macOS'
```

Never omit `-only-testing:` on a `test` action that can reach `ConsoleUITests`.

Run the entire UITest suite only when Christopher explicitly asks for it.
